# Project Core

Corporate Knowledge Portal — maintainable production app, not a demo page.

## Priorities (descending)

1. Architecture correctness
2. Data & admin security
3. Content management simplicity
4. Maintainability
5. Accessibility
6. Performance
7. Visual quality
8. Appropriate animation

Never sacrifice architecture or accessibility for visual effects.

## Phase discipline

- Execute **only the assigned phase or vertical slice**.
- After each phase: typecheck → lint → tests → production build → manual check → report → **STOP**.
- Do not start the next phase without an explicit new task.

## Hard bans

- No hardcoded articles, categories, section names, users, admin emails, Google IDs, Doc/Sheet IDs, Drive paths, dates, prompts, learning paths, secrets, or env config in app code.
- Separate test data from production data explicitly.
- No UI / Firebase / Firestore / Google API wiring / UI libraries / deploy / content migration until the assigned phase requires it.
- Prior HTML source materials are **content text only** — never CSS, JS, layout, components, animations, or design reference.

## Access model

- Public: read published content only; no registration, profiles, or personal cabinets.
- Admin/editor: Google Sign-In; **server-side** role checks on every admin API; audit every admin action.
- Client-side auth checks are never sufficient alone.

## Layers

UI → application services → domain → repositories → infrastructure adapters → external APIs.

UI components must not call Firestore or Google APIs directly.

## Skills policy (short)

- Call `pick-ui-library` before adding a UI dependency.
- Use `emil-design-eng` for UI craft; do not change approved palette or product architecture.
- Use `apple-design` only for gestures/DnD/physics/reduced-motion — not Apple visual cloning.
- Animation skills (`find-animation-opportunities`, `improve-animations`, `review-animations`, `animation-vocabulary`) follow their documented modes; do not mix audit and implementation in one run.

